#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kurso ng IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "Pagsusuri"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll analyze Grover's algorithm to understand how it works.\n"
"We'll start with what could be described as a *symbolic* analysis, where we calculate how the Grover operation $G$ acts on certain states, and then we'll tie this symbolic analysis to a *geometric* picture that's helpful for visualizing how the algorithm works.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susuriin natin ngayon ang Grover's algorithm para maunawaan kung paano ito gumagana.\n"
"Magsisimula tayo sa isang uri ng *simbolikong* pagsusuri, kung saan kinakalkula natin kung paano kumikilos ang Grover operation na $G$ sa ilang partikular na estado, at pagkatapos ay iuugnay natin ang simbolikong pagsusuring ito sa isang *geometric* na larawan na nakakatulong para maislarawan kung paano gumagana ang algorithm.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Solutions and non-solutions {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"
msgstr "Mga solusyon at hindi solusyon {#solutions-and-non-solutions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by defining two sets of strings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula tayo sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy ng dalawang set ng mga string.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  A_0 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 0\\bigr\\} \\\\\n"
"  A_1 &= \\bigl\\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = 1\\bigr\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set $A_1$ contains all of the solutions to our search problem while $A_0$ contains the strings that aren't solutions (which we can refer to as *non-solutions* when it's convenient).\n"
"These two sets satisfy $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ and $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n,$ which is to say that this is a *bipartition* of $\\Sigma^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang set na $A_1$ ay naglalaman ng lahat ng solusyon sa ating problema sa paghahanap, habang ang $A_0$ naman ay naglalaman ng mga string na hindi solusyon (na maaari nating tawaging *hindi-solusyon* kung maginhawa).\n"
"Ang dalawang set na ito ay tumutugon sa $A_0 \\cap A_1 = \\varnothing$ at $A_0 \\cup A_1 = \\Sigma^n,$ ibig sabihin, ito ay isang *bipartition* ng $\\Sigma^n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we'll define two unit vectors representing uniform superpositions over "
"the sets of solutions and non-solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tutukuyin natin ang dalawang unit vector na kumakatawan sa mga "
"uniform superposition sa mga set ng solusyon at hindi-solusyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert A_0\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_0} \\vert x\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert A_1\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert}} \\sum_{x\\in A_1} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Formally speaking, each of these vectors is only defined when its corresponding set is nonempty, but hereafter we're going to focus on the case that neither $A_0$ nor $A_1$ is empty.\n"
"The cases that $A_0 = \\varnothing$ and $A_1 = \\varnothing$ are easily handled separately, and we'll do that later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa teknikal na pagsasalita, ang bawat isa sa mga vector na ito ay natutukoy lamang kapag ang kaukulang set ay hindi walang laman, ngunit mula rito ay magtutuon tayo sa kasong hindi walang laman ang $A_0$ at $A_1$.\n"
"Ang mga kaso na $A_0 = \\varnothing$ at $A_1 = \\varnothing$ ay madaling harapin nang hiwalay, at gagawin natin ito mamaya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an aside, the notation being used here is common: any time we have a "
"finite and nonempty set $S,$ we can write $\\vert S\\rangle$ to denote the "
"quantum state vector that's uniform over the elements of $S.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa karagdagan, ang notasyong ginagamit dito ay karaniwan: sa tuwing mayroon "
"tayong finite at hindi walang lamang set na $S,$ maaari tayong magsulat ng "
"$\\vert S\\rangle$ para ilarawan ang quantum state vector na uniform sa mga "
"elemento ng $S.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's also define $\\vert u \\rangle$ to be a *uniform* quantum state over "
"all $n$-bit strings:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tukuyin din natin ang $\\vert u \\rangle$ bilang isang *uniform* quantum "
"state sa lahat ng $n$-bit string:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Notice that\n"
msgstr "Pansinin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle,$ "
"so $\\vert u\\rangle$ represents the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ "
"after the initialization in step 1 of Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon din tayong $\\vert u\\rangle = H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle,$ "
"kaya ang $\\vert u\\rangle$ ay kumakatawan sa estado ng register na "
"$\\mathsf{Q}$ pagkatapos ng initialization sa hakbang 1 ng Grover's "
"algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that just before the iterations of $G$ happen in step 2, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ is contained in the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ and moreover the coefficients of these vectors are real numbers.\n"
"As we will see, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ will always have these properties — meaning that the state is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — after any number of iterations of the operation $G$ in step 2.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibig sabihin nito, bago pa mangyari ang mga iteration ng $G$ sa hakbang 2, ang estado ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ ay nasa loob ng two-dimensional vector space na spanned ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ at bukod doon, ang mga coefficient ng mga vector na ito ay mga tunay na numero.\n"
"Makikita natin na ang estado ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ ay palaging magkakaroon ng mga katangiang ito — ibig sabihin, ang estado ay isang tunay na linear combination ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ — pagkatapos ng anumang bilang ng iteration ng operation na $G$ sa hakbang 2.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An observation about the Grover operation {#an-observation-about-the-grover-"
"operation}"
msgstr ""
"Isang obserbasyon tungkol sa Grover operation {#an-observation-about-the-"
"grover-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We'll now turn our attention to the Grover operation\n"
msgstr "Titingnan natin ngayon ang Grover operation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "beginning with an interesting observation about it.\n"
msgstr "simula sa isang kawili-wiling obserbasyon tungkol dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine for a moment that we replaced the function $f$ by the composition of $f$ with the NOT function — or, in other words, the function we get by flipping the output bit of $f.$\n"
"We'll call this new function $g,$ and we can express it using symbols in a few alternative ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isipin nang sandali na pinalitan natin ang function na $f$ ng composition ng $f$ at ng NOT function — o, sa madaling salita, ang function na nakukuha natin sa pamamagitan ng pag-flip ng output bit ng $f.$\n"
"Tatawagin natin itong bagong function na $g,$ at maaari nating ipahayag ito gamit ang mga simbolo sa ilang alternatibong paraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(x) = \\neg f(x) = 1 \\oplus f(x) = 1 - f(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & f(x) = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & f(x) = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(-1)^{g(x)} = (-1)^{1 \\oplus f(x)} = - (-1)^{f(x)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ and therefore\n"
msgstr "para sa bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ at samakatuwid\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_g = - Z_f.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that if we were to substitute the function $f$ with the function "
"$g,$ Grover's algorithm wouldn't function any differently — because the "
"states we obtain from the algorithm in the two cases are necessarily "
"equivalent up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibig sabihin nito, kung papalitan natin ang function na $f$ ng function na "
"$g,$ hindi magbabago ang Grover's algorithm — dahil ang mga estado na "
"nakukuha natin mula sa algorithm sa dalawang kaso ay kinakailangang katumbas"
" hanggang sa isang global phase.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This isn't a problem!\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the algorithm doesn't care which strings are solutions and which are non-solutions — it only needs to be able to *distinguish* solutions and non-solutions to operate correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Wala itong problema!\n"
"Sa simpleng pagsasalita, hindi pinapansin ng algorithm kung aling mga string ang solusyon at aling mga string ang hindi — kailangan lang nitong *makilala* ang mga solusyon at hindi-solusyon para gumana nang tama.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Action of the Grover operation {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"
msgstr "Kilos ng Grover operation {#action-of-the-grover-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider the action of $G$ on the quantum state vectors $\\vert "
"A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan natin ngayon ang kilos ng $G$ sa mga quantum state vector na $\\vert"
" A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's observe that the operation $Z_f$ has a very simple action on "
"$\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, pansinin na ang operation na $Z_f$ ay may napakasimpleng kilos sa "
"$\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"The operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalawa, mayroon tayong operation na $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"Ang operation na $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ ay tinukoy bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"again for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ and a convenient alternative way to"
" express this operation is like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"muli para sa bawat string na $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ at ang isang maginhawang "
"alternatibong paraan ng pagpapahayag ng operation na ito ay ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} = 2 \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to verify that this expression agrees with the definition of "
"$Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ is to evaluate its action on standard basis states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang simpleng paraan para i-verify na ang expression na ito ay naaayon "
"sa kahulugan ng $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ ay ang suriin ang kilos nito sa mga "
"standard basis state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ can therefore"
" be written like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operation na $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}$ ay "
"maaaring isulat nang ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0^n \\rangle \\langle 0^n \\vert H^{\\otimes n} - \\mathbb{I} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"using the same notation, $\\vert u \\rangle,$ that we used above for the "
"uniform superposition over all $n$-bit strings.\n"
msgstr ""
"gamit ang parehong notasyon, $\\vert u \\rangle,$ na ginamit natin sa itaas "
"para sa uniform superposition sa lahat ng $n$-bit string.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we have what we need to compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"First let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"At ngayon mayroon na tayong kailangan para kalkulahin ang kilos ng $G$ sa $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"Una, kalkulahin natin ang kilos ng $G$ sa $\\vert A_0\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle -\\vert A_0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"  -\\vert A_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\biggl( \\frac{2\\vert A_0\\vert}{N} - 1\\biggr) \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "And second, let's compute the action of $G$ on $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "At pangalawa, kalkulahin natin ang kilos ng $G$ sa $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\bigl( 2 \\vert u\\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I} \\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert u\\rangle + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - 2 \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"      + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\\biggr) + \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\biggl( 1 - \\frac{2\\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\biggr) \\vert A_1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In both cases we're using the equation\n"
msgstr "Sa dalawang kaso, ginagamit natin ang equation na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "along with the expressions\n"
msgstr "kasama ang mga expression na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_0\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\langle u \\vert A_1\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1 \\vert}{N}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "that follow.\n"
msgstr "na sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In summary, we have\n"
msgstr "Sa buod, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  G \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  G \\vert A_1 \\rangle\n"
"  & = - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\vert A_0 \\rangle\n"
"      + \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} \\vert A_1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we already noted, the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ just prior to step 2 is contained in the two-dimensional space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ and we have just established that $G$ maps any vector in this space to another vector in the same space.\n"
"This means that, for the sake of the analysis, we can focus our attention exclusively on this subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng nabanggit na natin, ang estado ng $\\mathsf{Q}$ bago pa mangyari ang hakbang 2 ay nasa loob ng two-dimensional space na spanned ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ at napatunayan na natin na ang $G$ ay nagmamapa ng anumang vector sa space na ito patungo sa isa pang vector sa parehong space.\n"
"Ibig sabihin nito, para sa layunin ng pagsusuri, maaari nating itutok ang ating atensyon nang eksklusibo sa subspace na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To better understand what's happening within this two-dimensional space, "
"let's express the action of $G$ on this space as a matrix,\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mas maunawaan kung ano ang nangyayari sa loob ng two-dimensional space "
"na ito, ipahayag natin ang kilos ng $G$ sa space na ito bilang isang "
"matrix,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"whose first and second rows/columns correspond to $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ respectively.\n"
"So far in this series, we've always connected the rows and columns of matrices with the classical states of a system, but matrices can also be used to describe the actions of linear mappings on different bases like we have here.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang una at ikalawang row/column ay naaayon sa $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$ ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"
"Sa ngayon sa seryeng ito, palagi tayong nag-uugnay ng mga row at column ng mga matrix sa mga classical state ng isang sistema, ngunit ang mga matrix ay maaari ring gamitin para ilarawan ang mga kilos ng mga linear mapping sa iba't ibang basis tulad ng mayroon tayo dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While it isn't at all obvious at first glance, the matrix $M$ is what we "
"obtain by *squaring* a simpler-looking matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagaman hindi ito halatang makikita sa unang tingin, ang matrix na $M$ ay "
"ang makukuha natin sa pamamagitan ng *pag-square* ng isang mas simpleng "
"matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N} & -\\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_1\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_0\\vert}}{N} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{2 \\sqrt{\\vert A_0\\vert \\cdot \\vert A_1\\vert}}{N} & \\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert - \\vert A_1\\vert}{N}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = M\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix\n"
msgstr "Ang matrix na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a *rotation matrix*, which we can alternatively express as\n"
msgstr "ay isang *rotation matrix*, na maaari rin nating ipahayag bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} & - \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "para sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}}\\biggr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This angle $\\theta$ is going to play a very important role in the analysis "
"that follows, so it's worth stressing its importance here as we see it for "
"the first time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang angle na $\\theta$ ay magkakaroon ng napakahalagang papel sa pagsusuring"
" susunod, kaya sulit na bigyang-diin ang kahalagahan nito dito habang "
"nakikita natin ito sa unang pagkakataon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In light of this expression of this matrix, we observe that\n"
msgstr "Sa liwanag ng expression na ito ng matrix, mapapansing\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(\\theta) & -\\sin(\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^2\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\cos(2\\theta) & -\\sin(2\\theta) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\sin(2\\theta) & \\cos(2\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is because rotating by the angle $\\theta$ two times is equivalent to rotating by the angle $2\\theta.$\n"
"Another way to see this is to make use of the alternative expression\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay dahil ang pag-rotate ng angle na $\\theta$ nang dalawang beses ay katumbas ng pag-rotate ng angle na $2\\theta.$\n"
"Ang isa pang paraan para makita ito ay ang gamitin ang alternatibong expression na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\theta\n"
"= \\cos^{-1}\\biggl(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}}\\biggr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "together with the *double angle* formulas from trigonometry:\n"
msgstr "kasama ang mga *double angle* formula mula sa trigonometry:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"In summary, the state of the register $\\mathsf{Q}$ at the start of step 2 is\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\cos(2\\theta) & = \\cos^2(\\theta) - \\sin^2(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(2\\theta) & = 2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Sa buod, ang estado ng register na $\\mathsf{Q}$ sa simula ng hakbang 2 ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert u\\rangle\n"
"= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_0\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sqrt{\\frac{\\vert A_1\\vert}{N}} \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and the effect of applying $G$ to this state is to rotate it by an angle $2\\theta$ within the space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"So, for example, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"at ang epekto ng pag-apply ng $G$ sa estado na ito ay ang pag-rotate nito ng angle na $2\\theta$ sa loob ng space na spanned ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
"Halimbawa, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"G \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(3\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(3\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^2 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(5\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(5\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"G^3 \\vert u \\rangle &= \\cos(7\\theta) \\vert A_0\\rangle + \\sin(7\\theta) \\vert A_1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and in general\n"
msgstr "at sa pangkalahatan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"G^t \\vert u \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\sin\\bigl((2t + 1)\\theta\\bigr) \\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Geometric na larawan {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's connect the analysis we just went through to a geometric picture.\n"
"The idea is that the operation $G$ is the product of two *reflections*,\n"
"$Z_f$ and $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"And the net effect of performing two reflections is to perform a *rotation*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iuugnay natin ngayon ang pagsusuring dumaan tayo kanina sa isang geometric na larawan.\n"
"Ang ideya ay ang operation na $G$ ay produkto ng dalawang *reflection*,\n"
"$Z_f$ at $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n}.$\n"
"At ang net effect ng pagsasagawa ng dalawang reflection ay ang pagsasagawa ng isang *rotation*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's start with $Z_f.$\n"
"As we already observed previously, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula tayo sa $Z_f.$\n"
"Tulad ng naobserbahan na natin kanina, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_0\\rangle & = \\vert A_0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z_f \\vert A_1\\rangle & = -\\vert A_1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Within the two-dimensional vector space spanned by $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$\n"
"this is a *reflection* about the line parallel to $\\vert A_0\\rangle,$ which we'll call $L_1.$\n"
"Here's a figure illustrating the action of this reflection on a hypothetical unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$\n"
"which we're assuming is a real linear combination of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa loob ng two-dimensional vector space na spanned ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle,$\n"
"ito ay isang *reflection* tungkol sa linya na parallel sa $\\vert A_0\\rangle,$ na tatawagin nating $L_1.$\n"
"Narito ang isang figure na naglalarawan ng kilos ng reflection na ito sa isang hypothetical unit vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$\n"
"na inaasahan nating isang tunay na linear combination ng $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection1.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second we have the operation $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes "
"n},$ which we've already seen can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalawa, mayroon tayong operation na $H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} "
"H^{\\otimes n},$ na nakita na nating maaaring isulat bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} = 2 \\vert u \\rangle \\langle u \\vert - \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is also a reflection, this time about the line $L_2$ parallel to the vector $\\vert u\\rangle.$\n"
"Here's a figure depicting the action of this reflection on a unit vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito rin ay isang reflection, sa pagkakataong ito tungkol sa linya $L_2$ na parallel sa vector na $\\vert u\\rangle.$\n"
"Narito ang isang figure na naglalarawan ng kilos ng reflection na ito sa isang unit vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a second reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A figure depicting the action of a second reflection on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/reflection2.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we compose these two reflections, we obtain a rotation — by twice the "
"angle between the lines of reflection — as this figure illustrates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag sinama natin ang dalawang reflection na ito, nakakakuha tayo ng "
"rotation — ng dalawang beses ang angle sa pagitan ng mga linya ng reflection"
" — tulad ng inilalarawan ng figure na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A figure depicting the action of the Grover operation on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A figure depicting the action of the Grover operation on a "
"vector.](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-"
"algorithm/Grover_rotation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This explains, in geometric terms, why the effect of the Grover operation is"
" to rotate linear combinations of $\\vert A_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert "
"A_1\\rangle$ by an angle of $2\\theta.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapaliwanag nito, sa geometric na termino, kung bakit ang epekto ng "
"Grover operation ay ang pag-rotate ng mga linear combination ng $\\vert "
"A_0\\rangle$ at $\\vert A_1\\rangle$ ng angle na $2\\theta.$\n"
